# Refinement-based game semantics

## Setup

1. Clone this project and its submodules,
```bash
git clone --recurse-submodules git@github.com:CertiKOS/rbgs.git
```

2. Create a local switch and install all dependencies using `opam`,
```bash
cd rbgs
opam switch create . --repositories=default,rocq-released=https://rocq-prover.org/opam/released
```

3. Load local switch into environment variables,
```bash
eval $(opam env)
```
4. Our `configure` script will take care of retrieving the git submodule
   for Coqrel, and will configure and pre-build it:
```bash
./configure
```
At this point make sure there were no error messages. This branch builds
with Rocq 9.2 and Stdlib 9.2 (see `rocq-rbgs.opam`); the CompCert(O)
integration has been removed.

5. If the configuration was successful you should be able to build the
   development using `make`. We recommend using the `-jN` option to enable
   parallel jobs. For example on my 8-cores machine:
```bash
make -j8
```
